              "description": "Identifies `gitsync sync` and `gitsync run`, which force-push and prune every configured repo's branches and tags to GitHub so the two sides end up identical, and can eventually delete the GitHub mirror once a repo disappears from the source (subject to gitsync's own delete_grace and delete_limit safeguards). `run --dry-run` reports what would happen without pushing or deleting anything and is treated as safe. `sync` also accepts --dry-run, but takes positional repo names and Go's flag parser stops at the first one, so `gitsync sync owner/name --dry-run` silently runs live; that ordering cannot be told apart from a working dry run here, so `sync --dry-run` stays reviewed.",
